{"id":"u-c5b985ae-4ca8-4ede-bdc4-52063809e158","src":"community","title":"Dev's PHUL Evolved: Science-Backed Strength & Size","author":"Dev A.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/zOJbdw-dev-modified-phul","desc":"Dev's Modified PHUL takes the proven Power Hypertrophy Upper Lower framework and refines it with what current hypertrophy and strength research actually supports — not just more exercises, but the right ones, placed in the right order.\n\nThe core stays true to PHUL: two power days and two hypertrophy days, split between upper and lower body, built around free-weight compound lifts — squat, bench, Romanian deadlift, and overhead press — for real strength progression alongside size.\n\nWhat sets this version apart is precision. Squat and deadlift are split across separate lower days for full recovery between the two most demanding compound lifts. Every major muscle group gets both a compound and a targeted isolation angle where the science actually supports it — chest gets pressing plus a stretch-position fly, glutes get squat/RDL plus a dedicated hip thrust for peak-contraction activation, and biceps/triceps each get two variations training different portions of the range. Rear delts, forearms, hip stability, and abs — commonly skipped in standard templates — are fully covered without adding junk volume elsewhere.\n\nEvery exercise is sequenced by fatigue management: heaviest, most technical compounds first while you're fresh, isolation and small-muscle work last. RIR (Reps in Reserve) targets are built into every set, since effort relative to failure is as strong a predictor of growth as total volume.\n\nBuilt for lifters who want a program with zero blind spots — real strength, complete muscle coverage, and no wasted effort.","level":["Beginner","Novice","Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Athletics","Muscle","Strength","Women's"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":1,"updated":"2026-10-11T22:21:11.533Z","variations